{
  "title": "HealthAI — Clinical Safety",
  "uid": "healthai-clinical",
  "tags": ["healthai", "clinical"],
  "timezone": "Africa/Johannesburg",
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": { "from": "now-24h", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "modality",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": "Prometheus",
        "query": "label_values(healthai_scan_submissions_total, modality)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": { "text": "All", "value": "$__all" }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Read this first",
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**These panels show what the models did, not whether they were right.** Correctness needs adjudicated outcomes and lives at `GET /api/models/performance`, which updates over days, not seconds.\n\nA refusal is safe — the scan reached a human. A *wrong answer* is not, and the panel that would show one is **Flagged-positive rate**. Alert definitions: `ops/alerts.yml`. What to do about each: `ops/RUNBOOK.md`."
      }
    },

    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Clinical safety",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 4 }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Flagged-positive rate (catches a silently broken model)",
      "description": "No ground truth exists at inference time, so this is the only real-time signal that a model has stopped discriminating. Expected: tens of percent. Under 2% fires PredictionRateCollapsed (critical); over 80% fires PredictionRateSaturated. Not meaningful under ~50 calls in the window.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 14, "x": 0, "y": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (modality) (increase(healthai_scan_predictions_total{predicted=\"positive\", modality=~\"$modality\"}[6h])) / clamp_min(sum by (modality) (increase(healthai_scan_predictions_total{modality=~\"$modality\"}[6h])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "{{modality}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 5 },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "green", "value": 0.02 },
              { "color": "orange", "value": 0.8 }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Scans analysed (24h)",
      "description": "Denominator for the rate panels.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 5, "x": 14, "y": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [{ "expr": "sum(increase(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=\"analysed\"}[24h]))" }],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short", "decimals": 0 } }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Sent to humans unanalysed (24h)",
      "description": "refused_no_model + refused_no_consent + rejected_input. Safe, but it is radiologist workload that nothing else surfaces.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 5, "x": 19, "y": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [{ "expr": "sum(increase(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=~\"refused_no_model|refused_no_consent|rejected_input\"}[24h]))" }],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 25 }] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "piechart",
      "title": "What happened to submissions (24h)",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 10, "x": 14, "y": 9 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(healthai_scan_submissions_total{modality=~\"$modality\"}[24h]))", "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}" }
      ]
    },

    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Out-of-distribution refusal rate",
      "description": "Measured baseline on held-out same-modality images is under 4% (skin lesions 0.8%, benign lung nodule patches 3.3%). Sustained above 20% means the input distribution has moved and the published performance figures no longer describe this deployment.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 14 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (modality) (rate(healthai_ood_rejections_total{modality=~\"$modality\"}[1h])) / clamp_min(sum by (modality) (rate(healthai_scan_submissions_total{modality=~\"$modality\"}[1h])), 0.0001)",
          "legendFormat": "{{modality}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 0.2 }] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Consent take-up — automated analysis",
      "description": "Not a fault signal. A patient declining is a right being honoured, and the scan still reached a clinician. Watched because a sudden move usually means the consent copy or its placement changed, not that anything broke.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 14 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=\"refused_no_consent\"}[6h])) / clamp_min(sum(increase(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=~\"analysed|refused_no_consent\"}[6h])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "declined"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "percentunit", "min": 0, "max": 1 } }
    },

    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Capacity",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 22 }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Inference latency (p50 / p95)",
      "description": "Resident service answers in ~0.5s. The per-request Python subprocess fallback takes 8-14s — p95 above 5s means INFERENCE_URL is unset or unreachable and the fallback is carrying production traffic.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 23 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le, modality) (rate(healthai_inference_duration_seconds_bucket{modality=~\"$modality\"}[15m])))", "legendFormat": "p50 {{modality}}" },
        { "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, modality) (rate(healthai_inference_duration_seconds_bucket{modality=~\"$modality\"}[15m])))", "legendFormat": "p95 {{modality}}" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 5 }] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pipeline errors and saturation",
      "description": "Unlike a refusal, an error leaves no queued manual-review row — the scan may be lost to the patient entirely.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 23 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "sum(rate(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=\"error\"}[15m]))", "legendFormat": "error" },
        { "expr": "sum(rate(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=\"saturated\"}[15m]))", "legendFormat": "saturated" },
        { "expr": "sum(rate(healthai_scan_submissions_total{outcome=\"rejected_upload\"}[15m]))", "legendFormat": "rejected upload" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" } }
    },

    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Access control",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 31 }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Break-glass overrides",
      "description": "Bypasses the care-relationship check. Designed to be easy to invoke and impossible to invoke quietly — this panel is the second half of that. Each event names a clinician, a patient and a stated reason in audit_events.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 32 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [{ "expr": "sum(increase(healthai_break_glass_total[1h]))", "legendFormat": "opened" }],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 3 }] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Care-relationship denials",
      "description": "Shadow counts what enforcement would have refused; enforced counts what it did. Shadow falling towards zero is how the derivation is judged ready to enforce. Sustained enforced denials push clinicians towards break-glass or shared logins, which is worse for privacy than the access they prevented.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 32 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "sum by (mode) (increase(healthai_care_relationship_denials_total[1h]))", "legendFormat": "{{mode}}" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short" } }
    }
  ]
}
